# Copy to .env.deploy (gitignored) and fill in for your own machines.
# The Makefile includes it, so `make install-serve` and `make publish`
# stop needing a wall of variables on the command line.
#
# Only MINI is required, and only for the targets that deploy to a
# second host. `make serve-local` needs none of this.

# The ssh target the dashboard is served from.
MINI=my-server

# Where that host publishes its site to, over rsync. Usually the same
# machine as MINI; it is a separate variable because publishing and
# serving are separate jobs.
AIDE_DASH_HOST=my-server

# Passed to serve.ts on the serving host. Both are optional:
#   ROOT          the directory scanned for .aide/project.yaml manifests
#   BIND          the address to listen on (default 127.0.0.1)
#
# BIND defaults to 127.0.0.1: the dashboard answers on this machine
# alone, and a proxy in front of it (docs/deploying.md, "HTTPS and other
# devices") is the one way in from anywhere else.
ROOT=/Users/me/develop
BIND=127.0.0.1

# Rarely changed — the defaults in the Makefile suit most setups.
# PORT=8788

# MINI_REPO is the checkout the SERVICE runs from, and the default is
# the dashboard's own (spec 223) — the one a code landing merges into
# and installs in before restarting the job. Setting this to a checkout
# a person edits puts the service back to serving whatever that
# checkout happens to hold; see README.md, "On a second host".
# MINI_REPO=.aide/dashboard/checkouts/aide/code
# MINI_SRC=.aide/dashboard/checkouts/aide/code/dashboard
# REMOTE_STATE=.aide/dashboard
# QUEUE_PROJECTS=aide
